# Signing keys and secrets — never in this repository, and it is public.
#
# The ONE keystore that is tracked is upstream's own development key, which arrived with the
# import commit and whose password is published in Telegram's open source. It signs debug
# builds and nothing else; the build refuses to sign a release with it, by name.
#
# The real release key lives outside every git tree (~/.keystores) with its password in the
# machine's vault. These patterns exist so that a copy landing here by accident is never
# staged. A pattern cannot untrack what is already tracked, so upstream's file is unaffected.
*.jks
*.keystore
!TMessagesProj/config/release.keystore
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*

# Python release validation caches
__pycache__/
